<title>NETHERLANDS: Unilever shares up 6.20 pct in Amsterdam.</title>
<headline>Unilever shares up 6.20 pct in Amsterdam.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Anglo-Dutch foods to detergent group Unilever NV jumped 19.40 guilders or 6.20 percent to 332.80 guilders within minutes of the 0830 GMT bourse opening, boosted by earlier announced fourth quarter results.</p>
<p>At 1.15 billion guilders the fourth quarter net profit at current exchange rates was at the top of expectations, which ranged from 869 million guilders to 1.15 billion, and well above the 690 million guilders of the year earlier period.</p>
<p>Dealers said the company's announcement from Rotterdam that conditions would be generally favourable in 1997 helped buoy the stock.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
